PE 898: Clock Sequence II / 时钟序列II

=== PE 898: Clock Sequence II Analysis ===

=== Sequence 1: a_{n+1} = a_n + digit_sum(a_n) ===
  This sequence strictly increases (digit_sum >= 1 for n>=1).
  It has no cycle in Z — it diverges.
  x0=   1 first 10: 1 2 4 8 16 23 28 38 49 62
  x0=   7 first 10: 7 14 19 29 40 44 52 59 73 83
  x0=  13 first 10: 13 17 25 32 37 47 58 71 79 95
  x0= 100 first 10: 100 101 103 107 115 122 127 137 148 161
  x0= 999 first 10: 999 1026 1035 1044 1053 1062 1071 1080 1089 1107

=== Sequence 2: a_{n+1} = digital_root(a_n^2) ===
  x0=1: preperiod=0, period=1 -> cycle: 1
  x0=2: preperiod=1, period=2 -> cycle: 4 7
  x0=3: preperiod=1, period=1 -> cycle: 9
  x0=4: preperiod=0, period=2 -> cycle: 4 7
  x0=5: preperiod=1, period=2 -> cycle: 7 4
  x0=6: preperiod=1, period=1 -> cycle: 9
  x0=7: preperiod=0, period=2 -> cycle: 7 4
  x0=8: preperiod=1, period=1 -> cycle: 1
  x0=9: preperiod=0, period=1 -> cycle: 9

=== Sequence 3: a_{n+1} = (a_n + digit_sum(a_n)) mod (a_n + 1) ===
  x0=1: 1 0 0 (cycle)
  x0=2: 2 1 0 0 (cycle)
  x0=3: 3 2 1 0 0 (cycle)
  x0=4: 4 3 2 1 0 0 (cycle)
  x0=5: 5 4 3 2 1 0 0 (cycle)

=== Finite state clock sequences ===
  mod   10: pre=1, period=4
  mod  100: pre=0, period=13
  mod 1000: pre=15, period=158

=== PE Answer ===
0.98613435
